  "physical_interpretation": "In 135Nd Table I, B(E2) is nearly identical between Bands A and B (~0.32 vs ~0.28 e2b2) even though the total mean lifetime tau is ~2 times longer in Band B at low spins (e.g. 1.46 vs 0.75 ps at 31/2-). Because B(E2) is proportional to p_gamma / (tau * E^5), maintaining equal B(E2) with double tau requires the partial rate factor p_gamma / E^5 in Band B to be approximately 1.7 to 2.0 times larger than in Band A. This illustrates that identical B(E2) strengths between partner bands does not imply identical level lifetimes, and that level lifetimes alone cannot be directly equated to transition strengths without branching and energy compensation."
